`reset_after_compaction`:

```rust
/// Forget the call history, because compaction replaced what the model had read.
///
/// A re-read after a compaction is recovery, not a loop: the session dropped the tool
/// results the model was working from, so reading the same file again restores them,
/// and it comes back with the same bytes because nothing about the file changed. The
/// call position is kept -- it is where the run is, not what it has read.
pub fn reset_after_compaction(&mut self) {
    self.failing_signature = None;
    self.consecutive_failures = 0;
    self.answered_signature = None;
    self.answered_hash = None;
    self.consecutive_identical_answers = 0;
    self.answer_capped = false;
    self.recent.clear();
    self.consecutive_cycle_steps = 0;
    self.consecutive_empty_results = 0;
}
